# Floor-presence39 reference and emulator source preparation

This preparation follows the root-generated immutable generator02 corpus at
`.build/cyd-vorbis-floor-presence-corpus-01`: matrix SHA
`4a66d9f6cefc4876eb3a89c0084baeaf6d19ad5455a16c449de21c0525927f86`,
manifest SHA`85b4042b179ca9177e1789ae41b4c0c3e29d6d1b7fd48e10a327b7fa1d92472f`.
Root recorded actual construction terminal0,39cases/546packets/971520PCM bytes,
9mono/30stereo and9constant-all-absent cases. This is construction evidence only;
neither reference decoder nor target has run in this preparation.

The preparer read/wrote source files, read the root's construction metadata,
produced complete adaptation diffs and parsed Python AST. No prepared module
was imported, no prepared function or control was executed, and no decoder,
compiler, SDK, QEMU, Git or device command was run. All30 host control methods
remain pending root execution. Their synthetic PCM/log/WAV/MD5 data is never
reported as reference decoding or emulator output.

## Complete reference workflow

`host_driver.py` is a focused successor of the existing strict dual-reference
driver. It requires the exact actual matrix/manifest, all39case descriptors,
complete raw/carrier equivalence, all four transition types, and complete78
recorded decoder commands. Each command explicitly selects `vorbis` or
`libvorbis` before the input. Rate/channels are never forced. Each decoder must
produce exact full PCM16 WAV and framemd5 packet PTS/durations/MD5. Full decoded
streams satisfy all predeclared silence spans and per-packet/channel nonzero
witnesses. The cross-reference bound remains2signed-S16LSB, selected before any
measurement. The driver retains all failures and unmodified streams. It freezes
explicit corpus/preparation/source inputs, without globbing unrelated `.build`
scripts around the new direct-child corpus directory.

`seal_reference.py` accepts independently reviewed ACTUAL host report, wrapper
terminal and matrix SHA arguments, plus this preparation's reviewed readiness
SHA. It requires successful actual39/78 host facts before creating a fresh
qualifier bundle. It writes concrete `pins.json` from those actual identities;
it does not invent future report hashes, replay PCM or run a decoder/qualifier.

The bundle's `recorded_qualification.py --profile floorpresence39` independently
replays all78 actual receipts, executable/capture identities, original/frozen
source bytes, complete WAV/framemd5 streams, every witness and both reference
streams under bound2. Apart from adding witness metadata and replacing the
inapplicable blanket nonzero predicate, its receipt/path/PTS/MD5/format checks
retain the existing strict qualifier. Only this newly completed39 campaign may
be qualified. Prior21 qualifications and unrelated NONPASS reports are not used.

## Target preparation and complete numerical comparison

`prepare_runtime.py` accepts explicit actual qualifier report/terminal hashes,
actual qualifier-bundle pins, original matrix SHA and reviewed source readiness.
It validates the actual complete39 qualification before creating output. It
copies all198 original corpus members without rewriting them, derives the exact
contract and independently recovers all234C arrays/39descriptors, including39
floor-mask arrays. It replays the full recorded reference binding with the exact
qualified helper bytes before publishing the first runnable target controller.
The `controller.template.py` here is deliberately unresolved and is not runnable.

The controller retains the prior mono21 build/context/source snapshots,
compile-macro evidence, exact SDK identity, public raw API, full PCM persistence,
QMP lifecycle and nine actual command receipts. The finite case mask explicitly
uses uint64_t/UINT64_C/PRIu64. Coordinator remains core0; worker remains
core1/priority3/stack16384. Production CYD setup/output bridge and all radio
sources are unchanged. This fixture app is not production firmware.

`seal_numeric.py` accepts ACTUAL complete target report, direct-tool terminal and
runtime-preparation hashes plus reviewed source readiness. It reads those
metadata files and seals a fresh numeric bundle without reading target PCM or
protocol logs. Its `compare_capture39.py` then independently verifies the entire
actual target command/source/context/protocol/file record, reconstructs the
sealed controller, recovers all39 full target streams, and replays all78 full
reference streams before comparing every original channel/packet/sample.
All reference and target silence witnesses remain mandatory. `policy39.py`
predeclares exact39case order, floor schedules and2LSB bound for both references.
It allows only the deliberately silent channels/packets, with exact zero checks
already enforced per frame by the reference reader and target protocol.
Alignment diagnostics are never applied as corrections. No fitting, truncation,
shift, resampling, padding, channel swapping or mono duplication is performed.

## Root execution order after source review and freeze

1. Run `test_controls.py` and `test_reference_numeric.py`, each with explicit
   `--matrix .build/cyd-vorbis-floor-presence-corpus-01/matrix.json` and
   `--matrix-sha256 4a66d9f6cefc4876eb3a89c0084baeaf6d19ad5455a16c449de21c0525927f86`.
   Retain each actual wrapper receipt/log and terminal. No pass is claimed here.
2. Run the reviewed `host_driver.py --matrix <that-matrix> --output <fresh-host>`
   with the actual command wrapper. Preserve an actual NONPASS unchanged.
3. Only if the complete actual host run passes, seal its reference bundle using
   `seal_reference.py --campaign <host> --outer <host-wrapper-receipt> --matrix
   <that-matrix> --output <fresh-qualifier-bundle> --report-sha256 <actual>
   --outer-sha256 <actual> --matrix-sha256 <above> --readiness-sha256 <reviewed>`.
   Review its actual pins/entrypoint before executing its qualifier with
   `--profile floorpresence39 --repository . --campaign <host> --outer
   <host-wrapper-receipt> --output <fresh-qualification>`.
4. After actual complete qualification, run `prepare_runtime.py --output
   <fresh-runtime> --qualification <actual-qualification.json>
   --qualification-sha256 <actual> --qualification-terminal <actual-receipt>
   --qualification-terminal-sha256 <actual> --reference-bundle <qualifier-bundle>
   --bundle-pins-sha256 <actual> --host-terminal <host-wrapper-receipt> --matrix
   <that-matrix> --matrix-sha256 <above> --readiness-sha256 <reviewed>`.
5. Review actual contract/data/controller hashes, then root may execute the
   sealed controller with explicit reviewed contract/header SHA arguments and
   known ESP-IDF6.0.2/Xtensa/QEMU paths. No NIC or physical board is needed.
6. After actual target terminal0, seal its numeric bundle with `seal_numeric.py
   --runtime <runtime> --target <capture> --target-terminal <actual-direct-tool>
   --output <fresh-numeric-bundle> --target-report-sha256 <actual>
   --target-terminal-sha256 <actual> --runtime-preparation-sha256 <actual>
   --readiness-sha256 <reviewed>`. Review the actual numeric pins, then run its
   `compare_capture39.py` with explicit repository/runtime/target/terminal/output
   paths and the same three actual SHA arguments. Any complete numerical
   NONPASS remains a rejection under the original bound2.

This is finite valid-input floor1 presence work. It does not claim completeG6,
Vorbis conformance, physical performance, radio integration, or codec root-cause
diagnosis. Deferred zero-guard, target Ogg EOF/reset/OOM, FLAC target-error and
AAC private-state work remains untouched. Focused raw source origins and all
adaptation diffs are retained for review; source-only integrity is not execution.
